# Authentication in HRIS — Full Walkthrough

This app uses **HttpOnly cookie authentication**: short-lived JWT access tokens and opaque refresh tokens are set exclusively via `Set-Cookie` headers. The frontend never reads or stores access/refresh tokens in JavaScript-accessible storage. Sessions are restored via `GET /auth/me` with cookies sent automatically (on non-public routes).

**Demo credentials** (after `npm run prisma:seed` in `BE/`): `admin@hris.com` / `password`

---

## Authentication method (summary)

| Layer | Method |
|--------|--------|
| **Credentials** | Email + password |
| **Password storage** | `bcrypt` hash (cost 10) in PostgreSQL |
| **Access token** | Short-lived **JWT** in HttpOnly cookie `hris_access_token` |
| **Refresh token** | Random 96-char hex string, **SHA-256 hashed** in DB, HttpOnly cookie `hris_refresh_token` |
| **CSRF** | Double-submit: readable cookie `hris_csrf` (`Path=/`) + `X-CSRF-Token` header on mutating requests; FE also stores token in memory from response body |
| **Session restore** | FE always calls `GET /auth/csrf` on load; `GET /auth/me` only when **not** on a public auth page |
| **Authorization** | RBAC: roles → permissions, enforced on BE and FE |
| **Multi-tenant** | `tenantId` in JWT + `X-Tenant-Id` header on requests |
| **Token storage (FE)** | No access/refresh tokens in JS; `tenantId` and CSRF token held in memory for headers |

---

## High-level architecture

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant User
  participant FE as React_SPA
  participant Vite as Vite_Proxy
  participant BE as NestJS_API
  participant DB as PostgreSQL

  User->>FE: Submit login form
  FE->>FE: ensureCsrfReady
  FE->>Vite: POST /api/v1/auth/login
  Vite->>BE: forward with credentials
  BE->>DB: find user, bcrypt.compare
  BE->>DB: create RefreshToken row
  BE-->>FE: Set-Cookie access + refresh + csrf
  BE-->>FE: JSON user only
  FE-->>User: navigate to dashboard

  Note over FE,BE: Subsequent API calls
  FE->>Vite: GET /api/v1/employees
  Note over FE: cookies sent automatically
  Vite->>BE: forward cookies
  BE->>BE: JwtStrategy reads access cookie
  BE->>BE: TenantGuard + PermissionsGuard
  BE-->>FE: protected data

  Note over FE,BE: Access token expired 401
  FE->>BE: POST /auth/refresh-token
  BE->>DB: revoke old refresh, issue new pair
  BE-->>FE: Set-Cookie new tokens
  FE->>BE: retry original request
```

